# =============================================================================
# ATLAS ASCEND — environment
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. Set the same value in Vercel under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit a real token.
# =============================================================================


# Mapbox public access token — must start with `pk.`
# Create one at https://account.mapbox.com/access-tokens/
#
# This is the ONLY environment variable Atlas Ascend requires. It is read in
# exactly one place (`getPublicMapboxToken()` in src/lib/env.ts) and serves both
# the browser map and server-side geocoding.
#
# Required token capabilities (a default public token has all of these):
#   styles:tiles  — vector tiles. WITHOUT THIS THE MAP RENDERS EMPTY.
#   fonts:read    — glyphs for map labels.
#   styles:read   — only needed by /debug/mapbox, which loads a stock Mapbox
#                   style for comparison. atlasNight is authored in this repo,
#                   so the production map never fetches a hosted style.
#
# URL restrictions are optional. Leave them off while getting started; if you
# add them later, the deployed production hostname must be listed or Mapbox
# will reject every request with 403.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means this value is inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD
# time and is therefore public by design. Protect it with URL restrictions,
# not secrecy — and note that changing it requires a rebuild, not just a
# restart.
#
# If unset, the app still deploys and runs, showing an explicit
# "MAP SERVICE NOT CONFIGURED" state instead of a blank canvas.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN=
